  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthen Evidence Based Migration Response through Enhanced Data Collection on Migrants Presence in Bosnia and Herzegovina and Capacitate the State to Process Returns of Migrants to Their Countries of Origin</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">At the end of 2017, Bosnia and Herzegovina (BiH) started seeing a large increase in the number of irregular migrants and refugees to the country. The overall objective of the response is to contribute to the improvement of the migration management and service provision systems in BiH by strengthening the data collection and analysis mechanisms on the volume, flows and profiles of migrants inside and outside the Temporary Reception Centres (TRCs) in the country, while also complementing the ongoing projects on assisted voluntary return and reintegration (AVRR) through IOM&#x2019;s AVRR programme in order to assist migrants to return home through the operational experience of IOM. IOM also continues with strong advocacy on readmission agreements between BiH and the countries of origin. The proposed intervention is building upon the ongoing efforts of the broader BiH Inter-agency Migration Response, and the AVRR projects.</narrative>
  </description>
